<title>NORWAY: Statoil renews charter deal with Navix.</title>
<headline>Statoil renews charter deal with Navix.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>State oil company Den norske stats oljeselskap ASA said it had renewed the charter for product tanker Navix Erica by 12 months to spring 1997.</p>
<p>Operated by Navix Line of Japan, the vessel has a cargo capacity of almost 40,000 tonnes, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>Statoil has chartered the tanker since 1992 for carrying condensate from Kaarstoe north of Stavanger to destinations including Kalundborg in Denmark and Rotterdam in the Netherlands.</p>
<p>Statoil said its shipping division had recently contracted to ship between five and seven condensate cargoes from Kaarstoe to Gdansk Refinery in Poland.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
